  "description": "# Sony PVM-1341\n\n13\" professional monitor from the late '80s and early '90s, among their first to feature the \"box\" design that would become standard. The PVM-1341 is a more economical equivalent to the PVM-1342Q and PVM-1343MD. Unlike those models, the 1341 is NTSC only and does not have support for PAL or Secam. It also uses a coarser pitch A class tube rated for 450 TVL.\n\n# Sony Playstation\n\nThe PlayStation (codenamed PSX, abbreviated as PS, and later PS1/PS one) is a home video game console developed and marketed by Sony Computer Entertainment. It was released in Japan on 3 December 1994, followed by North America on 9 September 1995, Europe on 29 September 1995, and other regions following thereafter. As a fifth-generation console, the PlayStation primarily competed with the Nintendo 64 and the Sega Saturn.\n\n![](https://bit.ly/4akk9JQ)\n![](https://bit.ly/4hii7fD)\n![](https://bit.ly/40zaGLx)",
